# Line endings are a property of THIS REPO, not of each machine's
# core.autocrlf. Added 2026-08-26, matching the admin and reader repos.
#
# What was wrong: core.autocrlf=true with no attributes file. Git wrote CRLF
# on checkout, every tool that edited a file afterwards wrote LF, and a file
# edited in place but never re-checked-out ended up half and half - which
# silently breaks multi-line edits, because a literal match picks one style
# and misses the other. An audit on 2026-08-26 found 362 tracked text files:
# the committed blobs were already 362/362 pure LF, but the working tree was
# 211 CRLF / 145 LF / 6 MIXED.
#
# LF is the canonical form here because it is what is already committed and
# what every tool in this stack writes. Do not "fix" this to crlf - that is
# the arrangement that produced the drift.
#
# No .bat/.cmd/.ps1/.sh files are tracked in this repo, so there are no
# endings-sensitive exceptions. ADD ONE HERE (e.g. `*.bat text eol=crlf`)
# before committing any such file - a .bat with LF endings can fail to run.
#
# NOTE: this does NOT reach into src/common. A submodule is its own repo and
# carries its own attributes file.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touched, never diffed as text. `text=auto` already
# detects most of these, but being explicit means a detection miss cannot
# corrupt one by rewriting its bytes.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.zip   binary
*.xlsx  binary
